00:51:14.156 --> 00:51:18.350
So NeuroSAT at least
trained on SR uniform (10,

00:51:18.351 --> 00:51:21.280
40) is never confident in unSAT.

00:51:21.281 --> 00:51:22.700
It searches indefinitely.

00:51:22.701 --> 00:51:24.190
It searches poorly indefinitely,

00:51:24.191 --> 00:51:25.860
meaning it stopped taking

00:51:25.861 --> 00:51:29.120
big moves and it gets stuck
but it searches indefinitely.

00:51:29.121 --> 00:51:30.480
And it always guesses

00:51:30.481 --> 00:51:33.700
low confidence unSAT
until it finds a solution.

00:51:33.701 --> 00:51:37.760
Now, detecting SAT and unSAT
are very different problems.

00:51:37.761 --> 00:51:39.860
Now, proofs of SAT are
just variable assignments.

00:51:39.861 --> 00:51:43.295
In particular, they
fit in NeuroSAT memory.

00:51:43.296 --> 00:51:46.375
NeuroSAT has a memory

00:51:46.376 --> 00:51:48.795
as a couple of floats
for each literal.

00:51:48.796 --> 00:51:51.720
And it just needs to
represent a bit mask on

00:51:51.721 --> 00:51:53.370
those embeddings to be

00:51:53.371 --> 00:51:55.435
able to encode
the satisfying assignment.

00:51:55.436 --> 00:51:57.600
Whereas proofs of unSAT vary.

00:51:57.601 --> 00:51:59.650
So there are some
trivial proofs of unSAT.

00:51:59.651 --> 00:52:02.640
So, any formula no
matter how big if it has

00:52:02.641 --> 00:52:06.150
the clause X1 and the cause
not X1 is unsatisfiable.

00:52:06.151 --> 00:52:07.730
You don't have to
look at the rest of

00:52:07.731 --> 00:52:09.780
the problem to know
it's unsatisfiable.

00:52:09.781 --> 00:52:12.250
But others require
exponential time or

00:52:12.251 --> 00:52:14.860
space to establish
unsatisfiability.

00:52:14.861 --> 00:52:18.160
In some proof calculus
where the objects are

00:52:18.161 --> 00:52:20.180
potentially unbounded
in particular

00:52:20.181 --> 00:52:21.730
will not fit in
NeuroSAT's memory.

00:52:21.731 --> 00:52:24.950
So even if it was able to
use some kind of stack,

00:52:24.951 --> 00:52:26.740
data structure we wouldn't
be able to trivially

00:52:26.741 --> 00:52:29.110
decode proofs because they

00:52:29.111 --> 00:52:33.925
won't even fit in the final
embeddings for NeuroSAT.

00:52:33.926 --> 00:52:36.395
But, we hypothesize it if

00:52:36.396 --> 00:52:37.800
the unsatisfiable problems in

00:52:37.801 --> 00:52:40.320
the trainings set
have short proofs,

00:52:40.321 --> 00:52:42.300
NeuroSAT will
learn to find them.

00:52:42.301 --> 00:52:44.070
And to test this we generated

00:52:44.071 --> 00:52:46.095
the data set where like SR of N,

00:52:46.096 --> 00:52:47.400
the data comes in pairs,

00:52:47.401 --> 00:52:48.825
one SAT and one unSAT,

00:52:48.826 --> 00:52:50.160
and they differ by negating a

00:52:50.161 --> 00:52:52.000
single literal and
a single clause,

00:52:52.001 --> 00:52:53.560
but this time by construction,

00:52:53.561 --> 00:52:56.565
the unSAT problems
have small unSAT cores.

00:52:56.566 --> 00:52:58.900
And we do this in a simple way,

00:52:58.901 --> 00:53:01.090
we define this new
distribution SRC(n,

00:53:01.091 --> 00:53:03.690
u) where u is an unSAT core.

00:53:03.691 --> 00:53:06.585
And we start with
the small unSAT core u,

00:53:06.586 --> 00:53:09.210
over a small number of
variables k less than

00:53:09.211 --> 00:53:12.610
